From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:14:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] mesa-tools: link libxml2.so.2 for the bundled libLLVM

  root/bin/mesa_clc: error while loading shared libraries:
  libxml2.so.2: cannot open shared object file

The bundled root/lib64/libLLVM.so.20.1 is linked against libxml2.so.2,
the soname of libxml2 2.9. This prebuilt ships no libxml2 at all in
root/lib64, and the mesa_clc wrapper puts only that directory on
LD_LIBRARY_PATH, so it has to resolve from the host.

On Arch the host has libxml2 2.15, whose soname is libxml2.so.16, so
nothing resolves. Symlink the newer soname to the old name. The wrapper
only SHA-256 verifies files that have a .sha256 beside them, and this has
none, so the symlink is not clobbered and not verified.

Shader compilation was verified to work with it, producing SPIR-V.

Note this is a soname alias, not the library LLVM 20 was built against.
Any mesa path that needs an ABI libxml2 2.9 symbol would fail; if that
happens the real fix is to bundle libxml2.so.2 here.
---
 root/lib64/libxml2.so.2 | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
 create mode 120000 root/lib64/libxml2.so.2

diff --git a/root/lib64/libxml2.so.2 b/root/lib64/libxml2.so.2
new file mode 120000
index 0000000..8dbab37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/root/lib64/libxml2.so.2
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+/usr/lib/libxml2.so.16
\ No newline at end of file
